+# Built-in categorisation table v2: v1's rules plus the maintained lists of R4 (UK card
+# acquirers, payment gateways, marketplaces and delivery platforms; business lenders and
+# merchant cash advance providers; own pots and savings; cash paid in; cash-withdrawal
+# wording; HMRC repayments; refunds; explained non-trading money in).
+#
+# Rules are ordered; the first whose pattern (or one of whose names) matches the
+# upper-cased description, whose `unless` does not, and whose direction matches the sign
+# of the amount wins. `names` are plain words matched whole, with any run of spaces
+# between words; `pattern` is a Python regular expression.
+#
+# Protected rules (returned DD, director, capital, shareholder, lender, HMRC) come first
+# and win over the case profile and firm rules; only a per-line override changes a line
+# they match (R21). The precedence is in src/cma/categorise.py. A rule may also have
+# `requires`, a pattern that must match too.
