+# An explicit move to or from the applicant's own pot or space ("TFR FROM POT CAPITAL
+# RESERVE", "TO POT HMRC VAT") is an own-account transfer whatever the pot is called, so
+# every protected rule but a returned DD has `unless: *pot_move` and leaves it to the own
+# pots rule below. Savings wording alone is not a pot move: "DIRECTOR SAVINGS" stays
+# director funding.
+#
+# Ambiguous wording never resolves to trading receipts: refunds, own pots and explained
+# non-trading credits are tried before the acquirer lists, so "PAYPAL REFUND" is a
+# refund and "STRIPE CAPITAL" a drawdown. Cash paid in is trading receipts (D31).
